11:- CHANNEL: the open groove inside the band, 6.8 mm wide, open toward the finger (`design/architecture.md:440`).
128:- **Join:** SW1 (up), SW3 (down), SW4 (toward the hand), SW5 (toward the fingertip) and SW2 (centre) to the head of FLEX1 (`band_flex_thumb`), with solder paste and reflow on a flat carrier [PROPOSED: reason, the head stays flat in the ring]. In model v6 the head is flat, 6.4 x 6.4 x 0.15, and lies on a flat stiffener of 6.4 x 6.4 x 0.075 mm under it, drawn as part of the ribbon (`design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md:250`, `design/architecture.md:795`); the flex maker bonds the stiffener to the head before this step [PROPOSED: reason, the stiffener holds the head flat during reflow; its material, stainless or polyimide, is the flex maker's, `design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md:250`].
162:- **Before:** the body has, per the model v6 (`design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md:275` to `design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md:282`): the two floor slots 2.0 x 0.6 from X -3.5 to X -1.5, Y -5.9 and +5.9 (model v6.2, architecture 17.27; before it 2.6 x 0.6) (`design/mfg/specs/body.md:89`), with their bottom at the Z of the size (table above); the round joystick opening 5.60 through the wall, its axis on the radial line at the joystick angle of the size, on the joystick side (v7, `design/look/s1/merged32h-report.md:21`), coated with the body in the same batch as the frame FRM1; the joystick pocket 7.0 along the finger x 6.8 round the band, open from the bore up to a flat roof at the radius of the size, with the channel left uncut over the joystick (`design/architecture.md:795`, `design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md:249`); the glass seat lowered 0.05 mm under the glass footprint, outside the panel pocket (`design/mfg/specs/body.md:82`); the two floor pockets, 1.0 mm holes and 2.0 x 0.10 mm membrane seats at X -11.77 and +11.77, Y -4.8 (`design/architecture.md:657`, `design/mech/mic-path/mic-path.md:71` to `design/mech/mic-path/mic-path.md:73`); no wall slots and no pad holes (`design/architecture.md:557`); the motor pocket 5.2 x 2.6 at the motor angle of the size (`design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md:273`).
185:- **Join:** first the frame FRM1 (titanium grade 5, 5.40 outer diameter, 4.80 bore, 1.30 long, coated gloss black in the same batch as the body) is bonded into the round 5.60 opening from outside the band with 3M Scotch-Weld DP420 Black epoxy, 0.10 mm radial gap filled all round (`design/bom.csv:82`, `design/mfg/specs/joystick-nub.md:23`). Cure: 24 h at 22 C with no heat, the room temperature cure of 3M's data sheet for DP420 Black (revision June 2024, page 3: 4,500 psi overlap shear on aluminium after 24 h at 22 C); no oven, because the membranes of step 11 and the gaskets of step 12 are already in the body. Then the round cap CAP1 (`joystick_cap`, Makrolon 2407 colour 901510, shank 4.40 and flange as one moulded part, `design/bom.csv:81`) goes in straight from the bore: the 6.90 x 6.40 flange rises through the 7.0 x 6.8 pocket (0.05 mm on each side along the finger, 0.2 mm round the band), the 4.40 shank passes up through the 4.80 bore of FRM1 with 0.20 mm radial clearance, and the flange stops under the pocket roof, 0.05 mm below it, held on all four sides by the roof round the 5.60 opening (`design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md:249`, `design/architecture.md:826`).
234:- **Locate:** the slot 2.1 x 0.6 mm (inside model v8, `design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md:482`; 2.0 x 0.6 in model v6.2, `design/architecture.md` 17.27; before it 2.6 x 0.6) and the ribbon neck 1.8 x 0.11 in it: the open area to fill is 1.062 square mm per slot [CALC: 2.1 x 0.6 - 1.8 x 0.11]. The slot's bottom lies deeper on larger sizes (Z -0.20 on US 7 to Z -1.85 on US 13, table above), so the length of slot to fill changes by size.
249:- **Join:** the liner LNR1 (`band_liner`), resin cast into the channel over the parts, 0.3 mm thick, closing the channel toward the finger (`design/architecture.md:440`, `design/mfg/specs/band-liner.md:15`). The resin grade is open (`design/mfg/specs/band-liner.md:43`). The mould core is a ring of the size's inner diameter (`design/mfg/specs/band-liner.md:37`) and presses on the four pads so they stay flush and free of resin [PROPOSED: reason, the pads must be flush with the liner, `design/architecture.md:559`]. At the joystick the resin fills under the stiffener and a 0.1 mm strip on each side of the pocket along its length, where the 7.0 mm pocket is wider than the 6.8 mm channel (`design/architecture.md:795`, `design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md:255`), up to the dam.
250:- **Locate:** the core sets the inner diameter; the band's two edge walls set the width 6.8 mm (`design/mfg/specs/band-liner.md:28`).
322:| K-A5 | The liner is said to be cast in place over the parts (17.3, band-liner spec), but the model puts each ribbon inside the liner with 0.075 mm of resin on each side, and the parts stand on that resin, reached through windows not yet drawn. A single cast cannot make a ribbon float 0.075 mm under parts that are soldered to it; the alternative, a laminate liner made first (S19), is not proven by any maker. | `design/architecture.md:440`, `design/architecture.md:587`, `design/architecture.md:517`, `design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md:81`, `design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md:85` | PROPOSAL: build the first bench housing (B8) with the cast-in-place route of step 21, where the 0.075 mm layer is the solder joint's own height filled by the resin, and measure the liner's thickness over the ribbon; the mechanical designer then keeps or drops the laminate. | OPEN: unchanged in model v5 (`design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md:117`); v6 adds the flat head on a stiffener with liner fill under it (`design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md:250`), which does not answer how the trunk is embedded. S26, S19. |
323:| K-A6 | Each ribbon has parts at its band end and a joint of 8 lands (FLEX1) or 7 lands (FLEX2) at its board end, and passes a closed slot of 2.0 x 0.6 mm (2.6 x 0.6 before model v6.2). So the board-end joint must be made after threading, with the board held above the block (step 16). The ribbon's slack needs room when the board goes down. | `design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md:69`, `design/bom.csv:76`, `design/bom.csv:77`, `design/mfg/specs/band-flex-tails.md:61` | PROPOSAL: reserve a free area beside each slot on the under face for one fold of the ribbon. | CHANGED: the model v5 keeps a free volume of 2.6 x 2.2 x 1.03 mm beside each slot, checked empty (`design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md:134`). Open: whether one fold fits that height (bend radius, K21, `design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md:159`), and the board layout keeping it free (S14). |
